.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt PLANMODE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm planmode
.Nd install, verify, and manage the canonical OpenCode Plan workflow
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
creates and verifies the symlinks, commands, skills, and global configuration
required for the canonical Plan-mode workflow.
It is POSIX sh orchestration over Lua 5.4 bytecode.
It does not mutate the repository except during
.Cm install
with explicit consent, and it does not force-push or rewrite history.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Cm install
Install links and the managed config key.
.Pp
.Cm verify
Verify the installed files and OpenCode discovery.
.Pp
.Cm upgrade-check
Require the tested OpenCode baseline.
.Pp
.Cm status
Print a read-only health report.
.Pp
.Cm backup
Create a timestamped config backup.
.Pp
.Cm restore Ar file
Restore the global config from a backup.
.Pp
.Cm uninstall
Remove managed links and the managed config key.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
See the manuals for make, mandoc, cvs, git, gpg, sh and lua5.4.
